PATCH 330: the mission-ACCEPT AI-object route into FUN_0000_0731 -- widen the SI/DI object-pointer params
of FUN_0000_b059 / FUN_0000_059a / FUN_0000_0539 from `undefined2` (uint16_t) to the 32-bit pointer the
asm registers actually carry.  Same class as patch 328's FUN_0000_0541 fix (`undefined2` = uint16_t,
re_out/ghidra_compat.h:30 -> a pointer passed through an undefined2 param is TRUNCATED to its low 16 bits
at the C call boundary; FUN_0000_0731 then dereferences the 16-bit stub as a host address -> a low-address
SIGSEGV).  Each fix is asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (DS=SS=DGROUP=0x1c00; CS=0).

(a) FUN_0000_b059 -- THE remaining mission-ACCEPT crash (chain: ...->FUN_1000_a0ab->FUN_0000_b059->
    FUN_0000_b112->FUN_0000_0731, fault ~0xa99a, ~1/15, layout-flaky).
    asm 0xb059:
        b059: 0e            push cs
        b05a: e8 b5 00      call 0xb112        ; b112 takes SI,DI; b059 does NOT touch SI/DI before it
        b05d: 2b 45 10      sub 0x10(%di),%ax  ; DI is the object b059 dereferences throughout
        ...(0x59(%di)/0x5b/0x45/0x26/0x40(%di))
    FUN_0000_b112 (asm 0xb112: push si; push di; lea 0x4(%si),%si; lea 0x4(%di),%di; call 0x731) reads
    (%di)-(%si) via 0731, so BOTH SI and DI are object pointers.  In the C, b059 calls
    FUN_0000_b112(param_3, param_4): b112's params are already `int`, so param_3 = SI, param_4 = DI (b059
    already types param_4 `int`).  param_3 (SI) was `undefined2` -> the candidate object pointer was
    truncated to 16 bits.
    PROOF it is exactly this truncation (not a base-loss): the sibling walker FUN_0000_af1c walks the SAME
    object list (DAT_2000_9fbc @ DGROUP:0xdfbc) and calls FUN_0000_b112(piVar5, param_2) with piVar5 read
    the SAME way (`(int *)*table`) but passed through b112's full-width `int` params -> af1c is crash-free.
    The ONLY difference on the crashing FUN_1000_a0ab path is b059's `undefined2 param_3` truncating that
    same candidate pointer.  Widened undefined2->int (param_4 already int; b059 itself never uses param_3
    except to forward it to b112, so no other site changes).

(b) FUN_0000_059a -- asm 0x59a: push ax; call 0x731; pop dx; sub ax,dx; ... .  0731 reads (%si)-(%di)
    from the two register pointers; the C calls FUN_0000_0731(param_2, param_3) -> param_2 = SI, param_3 =
    DI.  Both were `undefined2`.  CALLER-VERIFIED truncation: the five direct callers pass
    FUN_0000_059a(<bearing>, (undefined2 *)&DAT_1000_d55a, DAT_2000_0b9e + 10) -- &DAT_1000_d55a is
    g_mem+0x1d55a (a full host pointer, DGROUP:0xd55a) and DAT_2000_0b9e is `int **` (its value +10 is a
    full object pointer); both were truncated to low16 by the undefined2 params.  param_1 (AX = reference
    bearing) is a genuine 16-bit value and is left `int` unchanged.  Widened param_2/param_3 undefined2->int.

(c) FUN_0000_0539 -- falls through into the shared FUN_0000_0541 tail (asm 0x541: call 0x731; push ax;
    call 0x927; mov ax,cx; pop ax; ret), which patch 328 already reconstructed.  0539's entry supplies the
    same SI/DI in registers (its enter/stack-copy prologue does not touch SI/DI); the C forwards them as
    FUN_0000_0731(param_6, param_7) AND FUN_0000_0927(param_2, param_3, uVar3, param_6, param_7) (0927's
    param_4/param_5 = si/di, already `int` per patch 328).  param_6/param_7 were `undefined2` -> truncated
    exactly as 0541's param_4/param_5 were before 328.  Widened param_6/param_7 undefined2->int.

All three widenings pass the full 32-bit pointer to FUN_0000_0731 / b112 / 0927 through the already-existing
implicit int->pointer conversion (same as patch 328's b112 `FUN_0000_0731(param_1 + 4, param_2 + 4)` with
`int` param_1 -> `uint *`).  Native == wasm (pure C type change).

SCOPE / HONESTY:
  - MISSION-PATH ONLY: b059/059a/0539 are in-mission flight/AI bearing helpers -> behaviour-neutral for the
    24 menu/settings verify flows (verified native 24/24 + wasm 24/24, native<->wasm 0-diff).
  - There is NO mission-cockpit DOSBox pixel reference; the acceptance bar is asm-faithfulness + crash-
    freedom + zero regression (per the project's documented mission-path doctrine).
  - NOT LANDED THIS ITERATION (named, per the "name the exact field" rule):
    * FUN_0000_0426 -- carries the SAME undefined2 param_3 truncation into 0731, but its C body is
      INDEPENDENTLY mis-rendered by Ghidra beyond the truncation: it substitutes FUN_0000_05b7's return
      (iVar1) for the %di object reads the asm actually does at 0x436/0x43c (`mov 0x8(%di),%ax` /
      `mov 0xa(%di),%dx`) and derefs `*(int*)(iVar1+10)` where the asm uses DI.  Widening param_3 alone
      would be a partial thread through a mis-rendered body -> it needs a full 0426 reconstruction, not a
      single width fix.
    * FUN_0000_a77e -- its object pointer is stored into 16-bit GAME-WORD DGROUP slots
      (DAT_2000_56f0 / DAT_2000_56f2 are `undefined2` accessors, re_out/fist.c) so the flat-model host
      pointer is truncated at STORE time (asm 0xa79e `mov %ax,0x96f0` legitimately stores a 16-bit near
      offset), PLUS the 0541 call carries int*-scaling errors (`piVar6 + 2` = +8 B and `param_5 + 2` =
      +8 B where the asm `lea 0x4(%si)` / `lea 0x4(%di)` = +4 B).  A faithful fix needs full-width shim
      storage for the object pointer (the game-word slot cannot be widened without clobbering the adjacent
      word 0x96f2) + the scaling correction across the whole walk -- a multi-field reconstruction, not a
      single asm-determined width.  It was not reached in any measured ACCEPT run, so a fix cannot be
      crash-confirmed this iteration.
